# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Code Skeptic Scanner - repository ignore rules
#
# The repository previously had NO .gitignore at all, so every test artifact
# (__pycache__, .pytest_cache, coverage reports, node_modules) would have been
# committed.  The entries below cover the artifacts produced by the backend
# pytest suite, the frontend Jest suite, the Playwright e2e suite, and the
# local development virtual environments.
#
# Generated artifacts only.  Nothing here ignores a source file, and that
# includes dependency lockfiles: a `package-lock.json` is the recorded
# resolution of a manifest, not an artifact of a test run, and ignoring one
# would make an install unreproducible and hide a supply-chain change from
# review.  No lockfile is committed today, so none is ignored either.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# --- Python bytecode / caches ---
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/

# --- Python coverage artifacts ---
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
coverage.json
coverage.lcov
htmlcov/

# --- Test report directories: the three the runners write, and the repository root ---
/reports/
backend/reports/

# --- Frontend test + coverage artifacts ---
frontend/coverage/
frontend/reports/

# --- Node dependency trees ---
node_modules/
e2e/node_modules/

# --- npm lockfiles: deliberately NOT ignored ---
# There is no `package-lock.json` rule here, and there must not be one.  A
# lockfile is the only artifact that records an integrity-hashed dependency
# graph, and `npm ci` refuses to run without one, so ignoring it would make a
# frozen install impossible for both `frontend` and `e2e`.  Neither package
# commits one today - both manifests exact-pin their direct dependencies
# instead, which frontend/src/test-utils/dependency-closure.test.ts enforces
# alongside the absence of this rule - but nothing here stands in the way of
# committing one.  See docs/testing/DECISION-LOG.md.

# --- Playwright / e2e artifacts ---
e2e/test-results/
e2e/playwright-report/
e2e/reports/
playwright/.cache/

# --- Browser/desktop evidence captured during verification runs ---
blitzy/screenshots/
blitzy/screen_recordings/

# --- Build output ---
dist/
build/
.vite/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Local development environments.
# `.venv-backend` is the CPython 3.9 virtual environment used to run the
# backend suite (see backend/requirements-dev.txt).  It lives inside the
# repository, so it must never be committed.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
.venv-backend/
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/

# --- Editor / OS noise ---
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.swp
